CURRENT PROGRESS
- confirmOrder / cancelOrder — guarded stubs → 501 "lifecycle RPC pending" until next migration batch.

Step 4 — routes (src/routes/payments.ts)
- POST /v1/payments — create (auth) → body→service→{order,…}
- GET /v1/payments/:orderId/status — status via view → effective_status
- POST /https://v1/payments/:orderId/confirm|cancel — wired, return 501 behind guard
- Verify /v1/payments already mounted in index.ts (packages route exists → yes)
Step 5 — tests
- Unit: code gen (alphabet/no dup charset), snapshot building, error mapping, expiry math
- Integration: create happy path, unknown package 400, cross-user 404 (mocks like existing test/unit/services/credit.test.ts)

Preface on table names:
public.payments (existing) is the high-level , encompassing payment ledger, a row will be created when a payment succeeds and user gets credited. Helpful to build the user's payments UI. 
public.payment_orders is for the payment-intent workflow where the user initiates a payment intent and go through the steps to pay for it and admin manually approve it.


(WIP) SQL - Create order lifecycle RPCs:- Update or create backend/supabase/migrations/<timestamp>_manual_payment_order_lifecycle.sql.
- Add a customer-confirmation RPC that moves only PENDING_TRANSFER to AWAITING_REVIEW.
- Make repeated confirmation idempotent.
- Preserve the original confirmation timestamp during notification retries.
- Reject confirmation for SUCCESS, CANCELLED, and EXPIRED.
- Add a customer-cancellation RPC that moves only PENDING_TRANSFER to CANCELLED.
- Record cancellation time and resolution metadata.
- Reject customer cancellation for AWAITING_REVIEW.
- Add an admin-rejection RPC that moves only AWAITING_REVIEW to CANCELLED.
- Record the rejecting admin and resolution time.
- Restrict all lifecycle RPCs to service_role.

Config - Configure payment and Telegram environment:- Update backend/src/types/env.ts.
- Add VietQR bank ID, account number, account name, Telegram bot token, Telegram webhook secret, and admin chat ID.
- Update backend/wrangler.jsonc with non-secret bank display configuration.
- Keep Telegram credentials and sensitive values in Worker secrets.
- Do not add Email handlers, Cron triggers, postal-mime, or KV bindings.

Service - Create payment schemas:- Create backend/src/schema/payments.ts.
- Validate package-list responses.
- Validate order creation input containing package ID and client-generated request ID.
- Validate order UUID route parameters.
- Validate customer confirmation requests.
- Validate customer cancellation requests.
- Validate order-status responses, including EXPIRED and expires_at.
- Validate lifecycle error responses.
- Return validation failures as ZodParseError

Create the payment service:- Create backend/src/services/payments.ts.
- Generate cryptographically random seven-character order codes.
- Retry order-code collisions with a fixed attempt limit.
- Resolve package data from the server-owned catalog.
- Snapshot the package label, price, and credit quantity into the order.
- Calculate the server-owned expiry timestamp.
- Call the atomic order-creation RPC.
- Return an existing order when the same user retries the same client request ID.
- Construct the transfer message from the order code.
- Construct the VietQR image URL from server-owned bank data, exact amount, and transfer message.
- Fetch orders by both order ID and authenticated user ID.
- Map database errors through AppError and PostgreSQL error-code handling.
- Expose customer confirmation and cancellation operations.
- Preserve safe behavior when concurrent requests race.

Create customer payment routes:- Create backend/src/routes/payments.ts.
- Add an authenticated package-list endpoint.
- Add an authenticated order-creation endpoint.
- Accept package ID and client request ID.
- Return order ID, order code, package label, credit quantity, VND amount, expiry timestamp, transfer message, QR image URL, and status.
- Add an authenticated customer-confirmation endpoint.
- Accept the order ID from the route.
- Move the order to AWAITING_REVIEW and initiate Telegram notification.
- Make repeated confirmation safe.
- Add an authenticated customer-cancellation endpoint.
- Allow cancellation only while the order is PENDING_TRANSFER.
- Add an authenticated status endpoint.
- Return status, amount, credit quantity, confirmation time, expiry time, and resolution time.
- Return 404 for missing and cross-user orders.
- Mount the router at /v1/payments in backend/src/index.ts.

Create the Telegram service:- Create backend/src/services/telegram.ts.
- Send a review notification after customer confirmation.
- Include order ID, order code, amount, credit quantity, customer identifier, and confirmation time.
- Include an explicit warning requiring bank-app verification before approval.
- Add approve and reject inline buttons.
- Keep callback payloads below Telegram’s size limit.
- Do not include secrets or full customer profile data.
- Treat Telegram network failures as retryable.
- Leave the order in AWAITING_REVIEW when notification delivery fails.

Make customer confirmation retry notification:- Store Telegram notification status as PENDING, SENT, or FAILED.
- When confirmation is repeated, avoid changing the order state or confirmation timestamp.
- Retry Telegram delivery whenever the notification status is not SENT.
- Return success only after notification delivery succeeds.
- Return a retryable gateway error when Telegram delivery fails.
- Keep the same order, status, and confirmation timestamp across retries.

Create the Telegram webhook:- Create backend/src/schema/telegram.ts.
- Validate Telegram updates, callback data, and order IDs.
- Create backend/src/routes/telegram.ts.
- Mount the route before global Supabase authentication middleware in backend/src/index.ts.
- Require the Telegram secret-token header.
- Require the exact configured admin chat ID.
- Return 403 with no side effects for an unknown chat.
- Route approve callbacks to the shared credit-grant RPC.
- Route reject callbacks to the admin-rejection RPC.
- Acknowledge callbacks after processing.
- Show ALREADY_GRANTED for repeated approval clicks.
- Show a clear error when the order is pending customer confirmation, expired, or already cancelled.

UI Data - Implement frontend payment hooks:- Create frontend/src/hooks/queries/usePaymentPackages.ts.
- Create frontend/src/hooks/mutations/useCreatePaymentOrder.ts.
- Create frontend/src/hooks/mutations/useConfirmPayment.ts.
- Create frontend/src/hooks/mutations/useCancelPayment.ts.
- Create frontend/src/hooks/queries/usePaymentStatus.ts.
- Poll every three seconds during the first 90 seconds.
- Reduce polling frequency after 90 seconds.
- Stop polling at SUCCESS, CANCELLED, or EXPIRED.
- Invalidate credit balance and history after SUCCESS.
- Surface retryable notification errors without discarding the active order.

UI Data - Implement active-order persistence:- Create frontend/src/lib/activePaymentOrder.ts.
- Store the active order under the authenticated user ID.
- Persist the order ID and creation time.
- Restore the order after navigation or reload.
- Check the backend before treating a restored order as active.
- Never trust local storage for ownership or authorization.
- Clear the active order after SUCCESS, CANCELLED, or EXPIRED.
- Clear it on sign-out or user change.
- Prevent order creation when an active order is successfully restored.

UI Components - Implement the manual-payment UI:- Update frontend/src/routes/credits.tsx.
